WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.940
Have you ever, like, actually thought about the ship of Theseus?

00:03.280 --> 00:05.220
Oh, right, the classic paradox?

00:05.240 --> 00:05.740
Yeah, exactly.

00:06.180 --> 00:10.080
Because philosophers have been arguing over this thing for literally thousands of years.

00:10.820 --> 00:12.140
The premise is super simple.

00:12.480 --> 00:17.120
You have this wooden ship, and, you know, over time the planks start to rot.

00:17.360 --> 00:19.260
Right, because it's exposed to the elements.

00:19.380 --> 00:19.560
Right.

00:19.860 --> 00:24.080
So you replace one plank, and then you replace another one, and another.

00:24.560 --> 00:28.320
And then a few years go by, and eventually you've replaced every single piece of wood,

00:28.320 --> 00:30.220
every sail, every single nail.

00:30.520 --> 00:33.140
The question is, is it still the same ship?

00:33.580 --> 00:34.080
And it is.

00:34.180 --> 00:36.560
I mean, it's the ultimate paradox of identity, really.

00:37.060 --> 00:41.620
Because we desperately want to believe that survival is about physical continuity.

00:41.960 --> 00:43.240
We want things to stay the same.

00:43.300 --> 00:43.780
We do.

00:43.980 --> 00:45.180
Think about a mountain, right?

00:45.260 --> 00:48.320
We look at a mountain today, we look at it a century from now,

00:48.400 --> 00:52.940
and we comfort ourselves with this idea that it's the exact same collection of rocks,

00:52.980 --> 00:54.260
just resisting the elements.

00:54.480 --> 00:57.660
But the reality is that the mountain is constantly eroding.

00:58.320 --> 01:02.840
And when you look at complex systems, whether that's, you know, your own body,

01:02.940 --> 01:07.080
or the company you work for, or even just the software running on your phone,

01:07.480 --> 01:11.820
that whole idea of static permanence just completely falls apart.

01:12.040 --> 01:13.120
It shatters completely.

01:13.480 --> 01:14.080
It really does.

01:14.220 --> 01:17.200
I mean, over the course of your life, almost every single cell in your body

01:17.200 --> 01:19.380
is going to die and be replaced multiple times.

01:19.460 --> 01:19.700
Right.

01:19.700 --> 01:22.980
Or if you manage a massive software architecture,

01:23.320 --> 01:26.600
you might end up updating nearly every line of code over a decade.

01:27.020 --> 01:30.080
A legal institution, like a democratic government,

01:30.640 --> 01:35.200
can completely change its laws, its representatives, even its physical borders.

01:35.480 --> 01:37.000
And yet it remains itself.

01:37.220 --> 01:37.640
Exactly.

01:38.320 --> 01:39.580
Somehow you are still you.

01:40.020 --> 01:41.860
The software is still the same app.

01:41.860 --> 01:43.720
The country is still the country.

01:44.240 --> 01:47.820
How do these things remain identically, fundamentally themselves,

01:48.120 --> 01:51.960
while literally changing every single component that makes them up?

01:52.020 --> 01:54.580
Which forces us to ask a really, really uncomfortable question.

01:55.080 --> 01:57.260
What is the thing that is actually surviving?

01:57.500 --> 01:57.720
Right.

01:58.020 --> 01:59.820
If it's not the physical matter, you know,

01:59.860 --> 02:02.020
and it's not the specific lines of code, then what is it?

02:02.020 --> 02:06.320
And that right there is the exact paradox we are unpacking today.

02:06.320 --> 02:10.440
We're doing a deep dive into this stack of material that was published just this morning.

02:10.920 --> 02:13.840
Today is July 31st, 2026.

02:14.240 --> 02:14.940
Hot off the presses.

02:15.420 --> 02:15.780
Literally.

02:16.660 --> 02:19.840
It is a mathematical monograph by a researcher named Flyxion,

02:20.280 --> 02:25.740
and it's titled Admissible Continuation, a Mathematical Theory of Persistent Systems.

02:26.280 --> 02:29.300
Now, full disclosure for everyone listening to this right now,

02:29.300 --> 02:32.060
this paper is incredibly dense.

02:32.480 --> 02:33.900
That is an understatement.

02:34.200 --> 02:35.200
Yeah, it really is.

02:35.260 --> 02:38.400
We are talking about hundreds of pages of, like,

02:38.520 --> 02:41.880
high-level differential geometry, topology, and category theory.

02:41.960 --> 02:42.420
It's a lot.

02:42.500 --> 02:44.140
It is deeply rigorous math.

02:44.140 --> 02:47.540
But our mission for this deep dive is to extract the core insights

02:47.540 --> 02:50.700
and sort of translate this highly technical math

02:50.700 --> 02:53.120
into a thrilling, intuitive shortcut for you.

02:53.240 --> 02:55.080
We want to do the heavy lifting so you don't have to.

02:55.220 --> 02:55.600
Exactly.

02:55.780 --> 02:57.920
We want to give you an understanding of the universal mechanics

02:57.920 --> 02:59.380
of survival and adaptation,

02:59.680 --> 03:02.220
but without completely drowning you in the equations.

03:02.440 --> 03:04.600
And the scale of Flyxion's ambition here,

03:04.700 --> 03:06.440
I mean, it really cannot be overstated.

03:06.520 --> 03:08.740
This isn't just some abstract mathematical exercise.

03:08.860 --> 03:09.540
No, not at all.

03:09.540 --> 03:13.100
It is a fundamental rethinking of what the word change

03:13.100 --> 03:15.160
actually means in our universe.

03:16.160 --> 03:18.200
Flyxion is proposing this unified theory

03:18.200 --> 03:21.120
that connects biology, software architecture,

03:21.620 --> 03:24.080
classical physics, and even institutional governance

03:24.080 --> 03:27.240
into one single cohesive framework.

03:27.900 --> 03:29.760
It's mind-blowing when you actually step back and look at it.

03:29.820 --> 03:30.340
It really is.

03:30.720 --> 03:32.700
The core argument is that persistence,

03:33.540 --> 03:36.800
just the sheer stubborn act of surviving over time,

03:36.920 --> 03:39.320
is a mathematical object in its own right.

03:39.700 --> 03:42.120
It's something worthy of independent investigation.

03:42.600 --> 03:45.960
So whether you are out there managing a chaotic tech stack,

03:46.180 --> 03:49.020
or you're leading an organization through a massive pivot,

03:49.020 --> 03:52.240
or, honestly, if you are just insanely curious

03:52.240 --> 03:53.660
about the nature of your own existence,

03:54.140 --> 03:56.580
this theory is going to give you an entirely new lens.

03:56.780 --> 03:58.180
A completely new way to see the world.

03:58.360 --> 03:58.540
Yeah.

03:58.860 --> 04:00.580
You'll start looking at how things survive

04:00.580 --> 04:02.160
in a fundamentally different way.

04:02.560 --> 04:03.760
So let's just jump right in.

04:04.240 --> 04:05.820
To understand how things persist,

04:06.320 --> 04:08.840
Flyxion argues we have to completely unlearn

04:08.840 --> 04:10.960
how traditional science looks at reality.

04:11.300 --> 04:13.060
Unlearn is the perfect word for it.

04:13.120 --> 04:14.120
And that unlearning,

04:14.280 --> 04:17.800
it starts with dismantling our absolute obsession with states.

04:17.800 --> 04:20.340
Right, because classical science,

04:20.480 --> 04:22.600
especially physics and computer science,

04:22.820 --> 04:25.920
is built almost entirely on this concept of states.

04:26.540 --> 04:28.940
Explain what we mean by a state in this context.

04:29.240 --> 04:31.160
So when we talk about a state,

04:31.380 --> 04:33.940
we mean a frozen snapshot of a system

04:33.940 --> 04:35.980
at a very specific moment in time.

04:36.680 --> 04:38.600
Like if you look at classical mechanics,

04:39.040 --> 04:41.760
a physicist wants to know the exact position

04:41.760 --> 04:44.540
and momentum of a particle at a specific time,

04:44.600 --> 04:45.620
let's call it time T.

04:45.960 --> 04:46.240
Right.

04:46.240 --> 04:47.440
That is its state.

04:47.800 --> 04:50.080
And the underlying assumption has always been

04:50.080 --> 04:52.600
that the state is the foundational reality.

04:52.860 --> 04:54.600
It's the primary mathematical object.

04:55.020 --> 04:56.380
And evolution or change

04:56.380 --> 04:59.200
is simply the act of jumping from state A to state B.

04:59.360 --> 05:01.480
I always picture it kind of like a strip of movie film.

05:02.160 --> 05:03.540
Traditional science looks at reality

05:03.540 --> 05:05.720
by isolating a single frame from that movie,

05:06.100 --> 05:07.000
putting it under a microscope,

05:07.200 --> 05:08.460
and just analyzing it to death.

05:08.580 --> 05:09.440
That's a great analogy.

05:09.440 --> 05:12.500
Flyxion's opening argument is that looking at that single frame

05:12.500 --> 05:16.080
is structurally inadequate if you actually want to understand survival.

05:16.240 --> 05:16.820
Well, this doesn't work.

05:17.060 --> 05:17.900
No, it doesn't.

05:18.160 --> 05:21.880
The monograph argues that the state itself is essentially an illusion,

05:22.200 --> 05:24.160
or at least it's a mathematical dead end.

05:24.720 --> 05:27.460
The fundamental primitive unit of analysis

05:27.460 --> 05:30.200
cannot be the isolated snapshot.

05:30.200 --> 05:31.400
It has to be the movement.

05:31.880 --> 05:32.180
Yes.

05:32.520 --> 05:34.220
It must be the transition itself.

05:34.420 --> 05:38.180
The trajectory between the frames is where survival actually takes place.

05:38.420 --> 05:40.500
I have to admit, I struggled with this initially.

05:40.740 --> 05:42.340
Oh, it's very counterintuitive.

05:42.640 --> 05:43.080
It is.

05:43.640 --> 05:45.200
Because, okay, think about it.

05:45.480 --> 05:46.500
If you're a business owner,

05:46.860 --> 05:49.680
your goal is usually to reach an optimal state, right?

05:49.840 --> 05:50.860
You launch a product,

05:51.080 --> 05:53.200
and you want to reach a state of high profitability.

05:53.200 --> 05:55.600
Or, if you were tuning a car engine,

05:56.240 --> 05:59.600
you are aiming for this optimal state of fuel efficiency.

05:59.800 --> 06:01.460
We are conditioned to want that stability.

06:01.580 --> 06:02.060
Exactly.

06:02.560 --> 06:06.520
So, are you saying that striving for a perfect, stable equilibrium

06:06.520 --> 06:09.820
is, like, mathematically the wrong way to look at survival?

06:09.940 --> 06:11.920
Well, let's test that idea with an example

06:11.920 --> 06:14.040
Flyxion uses from computer science.

06:14.120 --> 06:15.260
I think this will clarify it.

06:15.620 --> 06:17.860
Imagine you are diagnosing a computer, right?

06:18.320 --> 06:19.800
And you look at its memory state.

06:19.940 --> 06:21.020
Okay, I'm looking at the memory.

06:21.020 --> 06:23.640
You freeze the system, you look at the memory,

06:23.840 --> 06:25.680
and you see that it is completely blank.

06:25.880 --> 06:28.860
Just a vast, empty configuration of zeros.

06:29.160 --> 06:30.460
A completely blank slate.

06:30.700 --> 06:30.920
Yeah.

06:31.040 --> 06:32.640
Just zeros across the board.

06:32.740 --> 06:32.980
Right.

06:33.440 --> 06:36.180
Now, based solely on that frozen snapshot,

06:36.360 --> 06:37.360
that isolated state,

06:38.200 --> 06:40.340
what can you definitively tell me

06:40.340 --> 06:41.840
about the health of that computer?

06:42.660 --> 06:43.760
Well, nothing, really.

06:43.940 --> 06:44.840
I mean, it could be brand new,

06:44.900 --> 06:46.240
just sitting there waiting to boot up.

06:46.280 --> 06:46.680
Exactly.

06:47.240 --> 06:48.740
Or, on the flip side,

06:48.740 --> 06:51.520
it could be a catastrophic memory wipe

06:51.520 --> 06:53.300
caused by a malicious virus.

06:53.520 --> 06:54.080
Oh, wow, true.

06:54.300 --> 06:55.840
Or it could just be an intentional,

06:56.160 --> 06:58.000
routine garbage collection process

06:58.000 --> 07:00.180
that's clearing out old cache data

07:00.180 --> 07:01.200
to free up space.

07:01.420 --> 07:01.660
Right.

07:01.840 --> 07:02.820
Totally normal functioning.

07:03.140 --> 07:04.820
Or, perhaps the physical hardware

07:04.820 --> 07:06.720
just suffered a critical electrical failure.

07:07.300 --> 07:07.780
The point is,

07:07.860 --> 07:09.040
if you only look at the state,

07:09.140 --> 07:09.820
just the zeros,

07:09.940 --> 07:11.000
you have zero context.

07:11.680 --> 07:12.680
The state tells you nothing

07:12.680 --> 07:13.800
about what's actually happening.

07:14.020 --> 07:15.940
The state is mathematically meaningless.

07:15.940 --> 07:18.420
You cannot define what the system is doing,

07:18.500 --> 07:19.860
or if it is even surviving,

07:20.320 --> 07:21.900
without knowing the trajectory

07:21.900 --> 07:23.360
that led up to those zeros

07:23.360 --> 07:25.220
and the potential continuations

07:25.220 --> 07:25.900
that are available

07:25.900 --> 07:26.980
from that point forward.

07:27.200 --> 07:28.480
That makes so much sense.

07:28.720 --> 07:29.680
I kept thinking about this

07:29.680 --> 07:30.560
in terms of photography

07:30.560 --> 07:31.580
when I was reading the paper.

07:31.680 --> 07:32.000
Oh, so?

07:32.160 --> 07:33.440
Well, if I hand you

07:33.440 --> 07:35.020
this incredible high-speed photograph

07:35.020 --> 07:36.220
of a falcon,

07:36.920 --> 07:37.840
suspended mid-air,

07:38.320 --> 07:38.540
right,

07:38.920 --> 07:40.560
and its wings are tightly

07:40.560 --> 07:41.780
tucked into its body,

07:42.180 --> 07:43.300
it is a beautiful state,

07:43.380 --> 07:44.420
it's a gorgeous photo.

07:44.560 --> 07:44.860
Sure.

07:44.860 --> 07:47.260
But that exact same photograph

07:47.260 --> 07:49.480
looks entirely identical

07:49.480 --> 07:50.740
to a falcon

07:50.740 --> 07:52.980
that has just been shot by a hunter

07:52.980 --> 07:55.020
and is plummeting out of the sky.

07:55.180 --> 07:56.480
Oh, that's dark, but yes.

07:56.540 --> 07:56.740
Right.

07:56.940 --> 07:58.180
You literally cannot tell

07:58.180 --> 07:59.180
from the frozen frame

07:59.180 --> 08:00.880
if the bird is executing

08:00.880 --> 08:02.360
a masterful hunting dive,

08:02.440 --> 08:03.300
or if it is dying.

08:03.720 --> 08:05.100
The state is completely useless.

08:05.280 --> 08:06.400
Because it lacks momentum.

08:06.660 --> 08:07.000
Exactly.

08:07.520 --> 08:08.400
Only the transition

08:08.400 --> 08:10.520
the movie actually playing out over time

08:10.520 --> 08:11.620
reveals the truth

08:11.620 --> 08:12.640
about whether that organism

08:12.640 --> 08:13.480
is persisting.

08:13.480 --> 08:15.080
That analogy captures

08:15.080 --> 08:16.860
the mathematical essence perfectly.

08:17.360 --> 08:18.020
Because persistence

08:18.020 --> 08:19.620
is not about reaching a state

08:19.620 --> 08:20.820
and setting up camp there.

08:21.300 --> 08:22.100
Stasis is actually

08:22.100 --> 08:23.640
the opposite of survival.

08:23.860 --> 08:24.840
Which is so weird

08:24.840 --> 08:25.520
to think about.

08:25.760 --> 08:26.180
It is.

08:26.380 --> 08:27.580
But think of it this way.

08:28.200 --> 08:29.780
A perfectly stable system

08:29.780 --> 08:31.440
with absolutely no capacity

08:31.440 --> 08:32.240
for transition, say,

08:32.480 --> 08:34.740
a rock sitting in a complete vacuum

08:34.740 --> 08:36.000
is effectively dead.

08:36.000 --> 08:37.660
It has no mechanism

08:37.660 --> 08:38.620
to respond to any

08:38.620 --> 08:40.000
environmental perturbation.

08:40.120 --> 08:41.140
You can't react to anything.

08:41.300 --> 08:41.500
Right.

08:41.760 --> 08:42.460
But then,

08:42.600 --> 08:43.700
on the far opposite

08:43.700 --> 08:44.440
end of the spectrum,

08:44.740 --> 08:45.640
if you have a system

08:45.640 --> 08:46.380
with completely

08:46.380 --> 08:48.020
unconstrained variability

08:48.020 --> 08:49.140
where literally

08:49.140 --> 08:50.120
any transition

08:50.120 --> 08:51.560
is possible at any time,

08:51.900 --> 08:52.900
you just have chaos.

08:53.000 --> 08:53.700
The system just

08:53.700 --> 08:55.020
dissolves instantly.

08:55.220 --> 08:55.580
Yes.

08:55.760 --> 08:56.740
So survival is really

08:56.740 --> 08:57.860
this tightrope walk.

08:57.940 --> 08:59.500
It is the mathematical space

08:59.500 --> 09:00.420
between rigidity

09:00.420 --> 09:01.340
and chaos.

09:01.520 --> 09:01.700
Yeah.

09:01.700 --> 09:03.100
Persistence is this

09:03.100 --> 09:04.160
ongoing process

09:04.160 --> 09:05.520
of selecting transitions

09:05.520 --> 09:07.560
that continuously preserve

09:07.560 --> 09:08.560
the conditions required

09:08.560 --> 09:09.740
to make future transitions.

09:09.920 --> 09:10.360
I love that.

09:10.460 --> 09:11.200
Which totally shifts

09:11.200 --> 09:12.300
the objective, you know?

09:12.440 --> 09:12.680
Yeah.

09:12.820 --> 09:13.940
You aren't trying to pause

09:13.940 --> 09:15.540
the movie on a happy scene.

09:15.920 --> 09:16.740
You are just doing

09:16.740 --> 09:17.540
whatever it takes

09:17.540 --> 09:18.620
to ensure the film

09:18.620 --> 09:19.280
keeps rolling.

09:19.400 --> 09:20.160
That is the perfect way

09:20.160 --> 09:20.700
to phrase it.

09:20.820 --> 09:21.560
But, okay,

09:21.700 --> 09:22.680
if we aren't tracking

09:22.680 --> 09:23.680
isolated states

09:23.680 --> 09:25.680
and if the physical cells change

09:25.680 --> 09:26.980
and the software code changes,

09:27.180 --> 09:28.740
what is the actual thing

09:28.740 --> 09:29.500
we are tracking

09:29.500 --> 09:30.300
during these transitions?

09:30.300 --> 09:31.520
What actually has

09:31.520 --> 09:32.620
to survive the journey?

09:33.180 --> 09:33.520
This is where

09:33.520 --> 09:34.400
Flyxion introduces

09:34.400 --> 09:36.640
this really foundational concept,

09:36.900 --> 09:37.700
the boundary.

09:37.920 --> 09:38.400
The boundary.

09:38.560 --> 09:38.760
Yes.

09:39.240 --> 09:40.480
They formalize this

09:40.480 --> 09:41.860
as the primitive distinction,

09:42.220 --> 09:43.400
which is denoted mathematically

09:43.400 --> 09:46.560
as D equals S comma S complement.

09:47.100 --> 09:48.700
Which sounds super intimidating

09:48.700 --> 09:50.000
when you say it out loud like that.

09:50.000 --> 09:50.280
I know.

09:50.380 --> 09:52.260
D equals S comma S complement

09:52.260 --> 09:52.980
sounds complex,

09:53.100 --> 09:53.840
but it simply means

09:53.840 --> 09:54.840
that reality is divided

09:54.840 --> 09:55.680
into two sets.

09:55.960 --> 09:56.960
You have S,

09:57.120 --> 09:58.120
which is the system,

09:58.480 --> 09:59.660
and you have S complement,

09:59.660 --> 10:01.220
which means everything else

10:01.220 --> 10:02.240
in the entire universe,

10:02.380 --> 10:02.920
the environment.

10:03.160 --> 10:03.840
Just the system

10:03.840 --> 10:04.540
and the not system.

10:04.660 --> 10:05.100
Exactly.

10:05.520 --> 10:06.640
And Flyxion posits

10:06.640 --> 10:07.420
that a system

10:07.420 --> 10:08.820
only exists mathematically

10:08.820 --> 10:10.360
if it can be distinguished

10:10.360 --> 10:11.160
from its background.

10:11.360 --> 10:12.500
If you lose that boundary,

10:12.680 --> 10:13.500
you lose the system.

10:13.660 --> 10:14.340
So we're talking about

10:14.340 --> 10:15.500
drawing a line in the sand.

10:15.620 --> 10:16.620
Basically, yes.

10:16.860 --> 10:18.280
But the paper makes

10:18.280 --> 10:19.640
a massive claim here,

10:19.820 --> 10:20.740
and this tripped me out.

10:21.100 --> 10:21.960
It states that

10:21.960 --> 10:23.660
distinction precedes information.

10:24.700 --> 10:25.180
Yes.

10:25.500 --> 10:26.880
That is a huge pivot.

10:26.880 --> 10:27.820
Because I always thought

10:27.820 --> 10:28.420
of information

10:28.420 --> 10:30.520
as the base layer of reality.

10:31.020 --> 10:31.140
You know,

10:31.180 --> 10:32.460
we talk about DNA

10:32.460 --> 10:33.220
as information

10:33.220 --> 10:34.240
or binary code

10:34.240 --> 10:35.320
as the foundation of computing.

10:35.600 --> 10:36.440
How can a boundary

10:36.440 --> 10:37.480
come before information?

10:37.620 --> 10:38.560
To understand that,

10:38.620 --> 10:39.240
we have to look at

10:39.240 --> 10:40.040
how information

10:40.040 --> 10:41.180
is actually defined

10:41.180 --> 10:43.080
in formal information theory,

10:43.500 --> 10:44.360
which was originally

10:44.360 --> 10:45.860
formulated by Claude Shannon.

10:46.080 --> 10:46.260
Right.

10:46.340 --> 10:47.720
The father of information theory.

10:47.840 --> 10:48.060
Right.

10:48.480 --> 10:49.480
Shannon defined information

10:49.480 --> 10:50.320
essentially as

10:50.320 --> 10:51.700
the resolution of uncertainty.

10:52.660 --> 10:53.720
When you receive data,

10:53.860 --> 10:54.940
it eliminates alternatives.

10:55.260 --> 10:55.440
Okay.

10:55.600 --> 10:56.280
I'm with you so far.

10:56.280 --> 10:57.600
But imagine a universe

10:57.600 --> 10:58.260
that only has

10:58.260 --> 11:00.320
one possible state.

11:00.860 --> 11:02.640
Just a perfectly homogenous soup

11:02.640 --> 11:03.900
where nothing ever changes

11:03.900 --> 11:05.440
and absolutely everything

11:05.440 --> 11:06.260
is identical.

11:07.080 --> 11:07.960
In that universe,

11:08.100 --> 11:08.760
there is absolutely

11:08.760 --> 11:09.900
zero uncertainty.

11:10.140 --> 11:11.160
Because there's nothing to guess.

11:11.580 --> 11:12.160
Exactly.

11:12.540 --> 11:13.640
If every measurement

11:13.640 --> 11:14.560
you ever take

11:14.560 --> 11:16.440
yields the exact same result,

11:16.800 --> 11:18.000
there are no alternatives

11:18.000 --> 11:18.960
to choose between.

11:19.260 --> 11:20.120
And where there are

11:20.120 --> 11:20.840
no alternatives,

11:21.120 --> 11:22.600
there is zero information.

11:23.020 --> 11:23.940
Because there's literally

11:23.940 --> 11:24.860
nothing to communicate.

11:24.860 --> 11:26.000
It's like,

11:26.120 --> 11:27.920
if every coin you ever flip

11:27.920 --> 11:29.160
always comes up heads,

11:29.480 --> 11:30.760
a conflict doesn't give you

11:30.760 --> 11:31.480
any new data.

11:31.800 --> 11:32.660
That's exactly it.

11:32.900 --> 11:33.180
Therefore,

11:33.380 --> 11:34.300
the very existence

11:34.300 --> 11:35.060
of information

11:35.060 --> 11:35.960
depends entirely

11:35.960 --> 11:37.040
on the prior existence

11:37.040 --> 11:37.760
of a distinction.

11:38.260 --> 11:39.260
You must first have

11:39.260 --> 11:39.680
a boundary

11:39.680 --> 11:40.800
that creates a difference,

11:40.980 --> 11:42.220
a this versus a that,

11:42.500 --> 11:43.520
before you can even begin

11:43.520 --> 11:44.840
to quantify information.

11:45.280 --> 11:45.640
Wow.

11:45.640 --> 11:47.420
So before you can have

11:47.420 --> 11:48.360
genetic code

11:48.360 --> 11:49.900
or a legal document

11:49.900 --> 11:51.120
or a software program,

11:51.620 --> 11:52.800
you first must establish

11:52.800 --> 11:54.200
a mathematical border

11:54.200 --> 11:55.460
separating the system

11:55.460 --> 11:56.080
from the noise.

11:56.200 --> 11:56.400
Yes.

11:56.640 --> 11:58.280
And biology actually provides

11:58.280 --> 11:59.700
the most elegant illustration

11:59.700 --> 12:00.620
of this concept.

12:01.200 --> 12:02.820
Think about a standard

12:02.820 --> 12:04.440
biological cell membrane.

12:04.540 --> 12:05.560
Just the physical wall

12:05.560 --> 12:06.060
of the cell.

12:06.160 --> 12:06.340
Right.

12:06.420 --> 12:07.740
We often visualize it

12:07.740 --> 12:09.100
as this static wall

12:09.100 --> 12:09.840
like a balloon.

12:10.480 --> 12:11.880
But at the molecular level,

12:12.060 --> 12:13.780
it is incredibly dynamic.

12:14.340 --> 12:15.520
Material is constantly

12:15.520 --> 12:16.680
and violently flowing

12:16.680 --> 12:18.140
in and out of that membrane

12:18.140 --> 12:18.840
all the time.

12:18.940 --> 12:19.860
Like what kind of material?

12:20.080 --> 12:20.940
Water molecules,

12:21.320 --> 12:22.300
complex proteins,

12:22.540 --> 12:22.980
ions,

12:23.260 --> 12:24.340
metabolic intermediates.

12:25.000 --> 12:25.680
They are crossing

12:25.680 --> 12:26.300
that barrier

12:26.300 --> 12:27.560
millions of times

12:27.560 --> 12:28.560
every single second.

12:28.680 --> 12:29.540
It's just a highway

12:29.540 --> 12:30.260
of molecules.

12:30.420 --> 12:30.820
It is.

12:31.080 --> 12:31.360
Now,

12:31.480 --> 12:32.640
if biological survival

12:32.640 --> 12:33.540
required the cell

12:33.540 --> 12:34.060
to preserve

12:34.060 --> 12:35.800
its exact constituent matter,

12:35.800 --> 12:36.880
if it had to trap

12:36.880 --> 12:38.480
the exact same water molecules

12:38.480 --> 12:39.500
inside to remain

12:39.500 --> 12:40.440
the same cell,

12:40.960 --> 12:41.500
it would have to be

12:41.500 --> 12:42.440
totally sealed off.

12:42.580 --> 12:42.940
It would be like

12:42.940 --> 12:43.700
wrapping it in

12:43.700 --> 12:44.740
impermeable plastic,

12:45.220 --> 12:46.300
but it would suffocate

12:46.300 --> 12:47.640
and starve immediately.

12:48.040 --> 12:48.480
It would die

12:48.480 --> 12:49.220
within seconds.

12:49.840 --> 12:50.180
Instead,

12:50.460 --> 12:51.060
what the cell

12:51.060 --> 12:52.080
actually preserves

12:52.080 --> 12:53.140
is not the material,

12:53.420 --> 12:54.880
but the organizational boundary.

12:55.300 --> 12:56.340
The physical matter

12:56.340 --> 12:57.360
flows through the cell

12:57.360 --> 12:58.240
like water flowing

12:58.240 --> 12:58.860
through a vortex

12:58.860 --> 12:59.600
in a river.

12:59.820 --> 12:59.920
Oh,

12:59.940 --> 13:00.560
that's a great image.

13:00.920 --> 13:02.220
The water making up

13:02.220 --> 13:02.660
that vortex

13:02.660 --> 13:04.060
is entirely new

13:04.060 --> 13:05.000
every few seconds.

13:05.740 --> 13:06.860
The vortex persists

13:06.860 --> 13:07.960
not because it's made

13:07.960 --> 13:08.600
of the same water,

13:08.780 --> 13:09.800
but because the distinct

13:09.800 --> 13:10.660
pattern,

13:10.780 --> 13:11.780
the boundary separating

13:11.780 --> 13:12.700
the swirling vortex

13:12.700 --> 13:13.660
from the calmer river

13:13.660 --> 13:14.720
currents around it

13:14.720 --> 13:16.460
is actively maintained.

13:16.640 --> 13:17.800
I love that image

13:17.800 --> 13:18.320
so much.

13:18.680 --> 13:19.940
It clarifies so much

13:19.940 --> 13:20.520
of what Flyxion

13:20.520 --> 13:21.220
is getting at.

13:21.340 --> 13:22.320
Survival isn't about

13:22.320 --> 13:23.140
maintaining your

13:23.140 --> 13:24.440
specific physical form

13:24.440 --> 13:25.380
or hoarding

13:25.380 --> 13:26.220
your current atoms.

13:26.220 --> 13:27.400
It's just about

13:27.400 --> 13:28.140
maintaining your

13:28.140 --> 13:29.100
mathematical border.

13:29.100 --> 13:29.700
Exactly.

13:29.920 --> 13:30.760
As long as you can be

13:30.760 --> 13:31.460
distinguished from

13:31.460 --> 13:32.060
your environment,

13:32.360 --> 13:33.040
you are alive.

13:33.260 --> 13:34.460
Because information

13:34.460 --> 13:35.840
isn't this magical,

13:36.080 --> 13:37.060
independent substance

13:37.060 --> 13:37.760
floating around

13:37.760 --> 13:38.240
in the ether,

13:38.680 --> 13:39.900
it emerges purely

13:39.900 --> 13:41.300
as a quantitative metric

13:41.300 --> 13:42.420
of distinguishability.

13:43.220 --> 13:44.200
Persistence is simply

13:44.200 --> 13:45.020
the act of keeping

13:45.020 --> 13:46.320
the system distinguishable

13:46.320 --> 13:47.380
from the background noise

13:47.380 --> 13:48.380
as it moves from

13:48.380 --> 13:49.000
one transition

13:49.000 --> 13:49.660
to the next.

13:50.040 --> 13:50.380
But wait,

13:50.620 --> 13:51.700
if survival is just

13:51.700 --> 13:52.480
about maintaining

13:52.480 --> 13:53.100
a distinction,

13:53.620 --> 13:55.500
that begs a massive

13:55.500 --> 13:56.220
philosophical

13:56.220 --> 13:57.720
and mathematical question,

13:57.820 --> 13:59.740
which is who or what

13:59.740 --> 14:00.800
is doing the distinguishing?

14:00.920 --> 14:01.080
I mean,

14:01.340 --> 14:02.540
a border on a map

14:02.540 --> 14:03.500
only exists because

14:03.500 --> 14:04.320
a human being

14:04.320 --> 14:05.160
is looking at the map

14:05.160 --> 14:05.940
and agreeing that

14:05.940 --> 14:06.540
the ink line

14:06.540 --> 14:07.180
means something.

14:07.400 --> 14:08.320
So in this mathematical

14:08.320 --> 14:08.660
theory,

14:08.760 --> 14:09.580
who is the observer?

14:10.580 --> 14:11.660
That is the pivotal pivot

14:11.660 --> 14:12.820
of the entire monograph.

14:12.960 --> 14:13.520
That is such an

14:13.520 --> 14:14.320
important question.

14:15.020 --> 14:16.220
A distinction is never

14:16.220 --> 14:17.080
an intrinsic,

14:17.440 --> 14:18.380
absolute property

14:18.380 --> 14:19.560
of a system floating

14:19.560 --> 14:20.160
in a vacuum.

14:20.540 --> 14:21.820
It is deeply relative.

14:22.600 --> 14:23.480
And to formalize

14:23.480 --> 14:24.160
this relativity,

14:24.680 --> 14:25.700
Flyxion introduces

14:25.700 --> 14:26.300
what they call

14:26.300 --> 14:27.660
the observation map,

14:28.080 --> 14:28.780
which is denoted

14:28.780 --> 14:29.760
by the letter O.

14:30.240 --> 14:30.840
So we are mapping

14:30.840 --> 14:31.400
the observer.

14:31.600 --> 14:31.800
Right.

14:31.980 --> 14:32.520
But we need to be

14:32.520 --> 14:33.280
really clear here,

14:33.380 --> 14:34.060
especially for anyone

14:34.060 --> 14:34.920
listening who hears

14:34.920 --> 14:35.740
the word observer

14:35.740 --> 14:38.120
and immediately pictures

14:38.120 --> 14:39.900
like a guy in a lab coat

14:39.900 --> 14:40.620
with a clipboard

14:40.620 --> 14:42.280
or maybe something

14:42.280 --> 14:43.160
out of quantum mechanics

14:43.160 --> 14:44.260
where consciousness

14:44.260 --> 14:45.280
affects reality.

14:45.440 --> 14:46.420
That's not what this is.

14:46.500 --> 14:47.440
No, not at all.

14:47.520 --> 14:48.160
You have to remove

14:48.160 --> 14:48.880
the human element

14:48.880 --> 14:49.440
from the word.

14:49.760 --> 14:51.180
In this mathematical framework,

14:51.280 --> 14:52.320
an observer is just

14:52.320 --> 14:53.140
any process

14:53.140 --> 14:53.840
of discrimination.

14:54.100 --> 14:54.900
Any process at all.

14:55.160 --> 14:55.520
Yes.

14:55.520 --> 14:57.200
A thermometer is an observer

14:57.200 --> 14:57.940
it distinguishes

14:57.940 --> 14:59.500
between a temperature gradients.

15:00.060 --> 15:00.800
A compiler reading

15:00.800 --> 15:01.680
source code

15:01.680 --> 15:02.740
is an observer

15:02.740 --> 15:03.460
it distinguishes

15:03.460 --> 15:04.700
between valid syntax

15:04.700 --> 15:05.820
and errors.

15:06.500 --> 15:08.080
A biological receptor

15:08.080 --> 15:08.740
on a cell

15:08.740 --> 15:09.420
is an observer

15:09.420 --> 15:10.140
it distinguishes

15:10.140 --> 15:11.100
between a nutrient

15:11.100 --> 15:12.120
and a toxin.

15:12.300 --> 15:12.740
Oh, I see.

15:12.880 --> 15:13.840
The observation map

15:13.840 --> 15:15.000
is simply a mathematical

15:15.000 --> 15:16.060
function that takes

15:16.060 --> 15:16.720
the chaotic,

15:17.280 --> 15:18.380
infinite mess of reality

15:18.380 --> 15:19.500
and groups it

15:19.500 --> 15:20.300
into categories

15:20.300 --> 15:21.180
that it is uniquely

15:21.180 --> 15:22.580
capable of distinguishing.

15:22.580 --> 15:23.780
And because different

15:23.780 --> 15:24.920
observers have entirely

15:24.920 --> 15:25.760
different sensory

15:25.760 --> 15:26.420
apparatuses

15:26.420 --> 15:27.520
or logical rules

15:27.520 --> 15:28.680
they draw entirely

15:28.680 --> 15:29.580
different boundaries

15:29.580 --> 15:30.620
around the exact

15:30.620 --> 15:31.300
same object.

15:31.440 --> 15:32.240
They absolutely do.

15:32.400 --> 15:33.480
The example in the text

15:33.480 --> 15:34.840
that completely solidified

15:34.840 --> 15:35.500
this for me

15:35.500 --> 15:37.080
was the digital image.

15:37.560 --> 15:38.620
The Photoshop example.

15:38.720 --> 15:38.940
Yes.

15:39.280 --> 15:39.920
Let's say you have

15:39.920 --> 15:40.780
two photographs

15:40.780 --> 15:42.200
of a mountain landscape

15:42.200 --> 15:43.260
saved on your computer.

15:43.600 --> 15:44.480
They look completely

15:44.480 --> 15:44.940
identical.

15:45.300 --> 15:45.920
Same cloud,

15:46.100 --> 15:46.580
same snow,

15:46.700 --> 15:47.200
same lighting.

15:47.200 --> 15:48.580
But on the second photo

15:48.580 --> 15:49.440
you open Photoshop

15:49.440 --> 15:50.160
and you change

15:50.160 --> 15:51.620
exactly one pixel's

15:51.620 --> 15:52.260
color value

15:52.260 --> 15:53.320
by a single

15:53.320 --> 15:54.780
imperceptible shade.

15:55.040 --> 15:55.500
You've altered

15:55.500 --> 15:56.820
exactly one bit of data.

15:57.080 --> 15:58.260
A microscopic deviation.

15:58.580 --> 15:58.780
Right.

15:59.100 --> 16:00.080
Now if you put

16:00.080 --> 16:00.840
those two images

16:00.840 --> 16:01.580
side by side

16:01.580 --> 16:02.180
on a monitor

16:02.180 --> 16:03.180
and look at them

16:03.180 --> 16:04.140
with your human eyes

16:04.140 --> 16:05.340
they are identical.

16:06.240 --> 16:07.380
The human visual system

16:07.380 --> 16:08.540
is one specific

16:08.540 --> 16:09.500
observation map

16:09.500 --> 16:10.700
and its resolution

16:10.700 --> 16:11.960
simply cannot detect

16:11.960 --> 16:13.220
that single pixel change.

16:13.440 --> 16:14.080
It maps them

16:14.080 --> 16:15.060
as the same state.

16:15.180 --> 16:15.560
Exactly.

16:15.960 --> 16:16.920
To your human map

16:16.920 --> 16:17.960
those two images

16:17.960 --> 16:18.680
are mathematically

16:18.680 --> 16:19.500
the same state.

16:19.860 --> 16:20.380
But if you take

16:20.380 --> 16:21.480
those same two files

16:21.480 --> 16:22.560
and run them

16:22.560 --> 16:23.400
through a cryptographic

16:23.400 --> 16:24.000
hash function

16:24.000 --> 16:25.940
like a SHA-256 algorithm

16:25.940 --> 16:27.020
which acts as a

16:27.020 --> 16:28.020
different observation map

16:28.020 --> 16:29.060
it will spit out

16:29.060 --> 16:30.200
two wildly different

16:30.200 --> 16:31.000
strings of

16:31.000 --> 16:32.160
alphanumeric characters.

16:32.520 --> 16:33.580
Because the cryptographic

16:33.580 --> 16:34.480
hash is designed

16:34.480 --> 16:35.500
to be highly sensitive

16:35.500 --> 16:36.440
to the exact

16:36.440 --> 16:37.640
binary sequence.

16:37.820 --> 16:38.380
Any change,

16:38.480 --> 16:39.000
Cascades?

16:39.500 --> 16:40.020
Exactly.

16:40.580 --> 16:41.300
To the cryptographic

16:41.300 --> 16:41.700
observer

16:41.700 --> 16:42.900
those two images

16:42.900 --> 16:43.980
share no boundary

16:43.980 --> 16:44.580
whatsoever.

16:44.920 --> 16:45.520
They are entirely

16:45.520 --> 16:46.500
distinct entities.

16:46.500 --> 16:47.600
That is a flawless

16:47.600 --> 16:49.020
illustration of the concept.

16:49.420 --> 16:49.960
The human eye

16:49.960 --> 16:50.920
and the cryptographic

16:50.920 --> 16:51.660
hash algorithm

16:51.660 --> 16:52.540
together form

16:52.540 --> 16:53.580
what Flyxion calls

16:53.580 --> 16:55.000
an observation family.

16:55.200 --> 16:56.140
An observation family.

16:56.220 --> 16:56.440
Okay.

16:56.800 --> 16:57.880
They are two distinct

16:57.880 --> 16:59.080
mathematical perspectives

16:59.080 --> 17:00.200
looking at the exact

17:00.200 --> 17:01.080
same system.

17:01.440 --> 17:02.420
And the crucial

17:02.420 --> 17:03.280
takeaway here

17:03.280 --> 17:04.620
is that this relativity

17:04.620 --> 17:06.100
the fact that

17:06.100 --> 17:07.140
the boundary changes

17:07.140 --> 17:07.720
depending on

17:07.720 --> 17:08.360
who is looking

17:08.360 --> 17:09.760
is not a flaw

17:09.760 --> 17:10.400
in the theory.

17:10.560 --> 17:12.000
It is the very engine

17:12.000 --> 17:12.940
of how the rules

17:12.940 --> 17:13.500
of survival

17:13.500 --> 17:14.180
are generated.

17:14.180 --> 17:15.200
I have to push

17:15.200 --> 17:16.020
back here though

17:16.020 --> 17:18.460
because if survival

17:18.460 --> 17:19.720
is entirely dependent

17:19.720 --> 17:20.440
on passing

17:20.440 --> 17:21.160
a specific

17:21.160 --> 17:22.120
observer's test

17:22.120 --> 17:23.440
doesn't that mean

17:23.440 --> 17:24.020
that all the

17:24.020 --> 17:24.700
fundamental rules

17:24.700 --> 17:25.260
of the universe

17:25.260 --> 17:26.220
are just arbitrary?

17:26.900 --> 17:27.280
How do you mean?

17:27.520 --> 17:28.860
Well, we treat things

17:28.860 --> 17:30.140
like the laws of physics

17:30.140 --> 17:31.580
or the strict rules

17:31.580 --> 17:32.720
of a programming language

17:32.720 --> 17:34.300
as fundamental truths.

17:34.700 --> 17:35.680
If a boundary

17:35.680 --> 17:36.600
only exists

17:36.600 --> 17:37.500
because a specific

17:37.500 --> 17:38.380
map is looking

17:38.380 --> 17:38.940
for it

17:38.940 --> 17:40.120
are invariants

17:40.120 --> 17:41.380
just made up constraints?

17:41.380 --> 17:42.200
Are we just making

17:42.200 --> 17:42.780
up the rules?

17:43.000 --> 17:43.560
The short answer

17:43.560 --> 17:44.100
is no

17:44.100 --> 17:45.220
but the mechanism

17:45.220 --> 17:46.000
of why they aren't

17:46.000 --> 17:46.460
arbitrary

17:46.460 --> 17:47.280
is perhaps

17:47.280 --> 17:47.880
Flyxion's

17:47.880 --> 17:48.620
most profound

17:48.620 --> 17:49.260
derivation

17:49.260 --> 17:50.460
in the whole paper.

17:51.040 --> 17:51.560
Walk you through it.

17:51.820 --> 17:52.300
Traditionally

17:52.300 --> 17:53.800
science simply assumes

17:53.800 --> 17:54.860
invariants exist

17:54.860 --> 17:55.600
from the outside.

17:56.020 --> 17:56.440
A physicist

17:56.440 --> 17:57.500
will look at a system

17:57.500 --> 17:57.960
and say

17:57.960 --> 17:59.040
energy must be

17:59.040 --> 17:59.560
conserved

17:59.560 --> 18:00.300
let's observe

18:00.300 --> 18:00.780
what happens.

18:00.840 --> 18:01.020
Right.

18:01.100 --> 18:01.620
They start with

18:01.620 --> 18:01.980
the rule.

18:02.300 --> 18:02.760
Exactly.

18:03.200 --> 18:03.960
A computer scientist

18:03.960 --> 18:04.380
will say

18:04.380 --> 18:05.420
this code must be

18:05.420 --> 18:05.900
type safe

18:05.900 --> 18:06.780
let's compile it.

18:07.160 --> 18:08.160
They impose the rule

18:08.160 --> 18:09.360
from the top down.

18:09.980 --> 18:11.420
Flyxion reverses

18:11.420 --> 18:12.160
the causality

18:12.160 --> 18:12.760
completely.

18:12.900 --> 18:13.740
Reverses it how?

18:13.940 --> 18:14.480
The monograph

18:14.480 --> 18:15.580
proves mathematically

18:15.580 --> 18:16.720
that invariants

18:16.720 --> 18:17.560
emerge naturally

18:17.560 --> 18:18.480
from the bottom up.

18:18.880 --> 18:19.860
They are the exact

18:19.860 --> 18:21.400
specific mathematical

18:21.400 --> 18:22.640
conditions required

18:22.640 --> 18:24.060
to keep the system

18:24.060 --> 18:24.940
distinguishable

18:24.940 --> 18:26.040
to its particular

18:26.040 --> 18:27.220
observation family.

18:27.840 --> 18:28.460
Break that down

18:28.460 --> 18:29.080
for me a little more.

18:29.440 --> 18:30.420
How does a law

18:30.420 --> 18:30.960
of physics

18:30.960 --> 18:32.860
emerge from an observer?

18:33.440 --> 18:34.060
Let's compare

18:34.060 --> 18:35.380
three completely

18:35.380 --> 18:36.160
different systems

18:36.160 --> 18:37.080
to see the pattern.

18:37.260 --> 18:37.540
First,

18:37.680 --> 18:38.180
a compiler

18:38.180 --> 18:38.920
checking software

18:38.920 --> 18:39.780
code for semantic

18:39.780 --> 18:40.400
correctness.

18:40.400 --> 18:41.260
Second,

18:41.700 --> 18:42.160
a physicist

18:42.160 --> 18:42.780
checking a

18:42.780 --> 18:43.280
thermodynamic

18:43.280 --> 18:44.080
system for

