26:28.860 --> 26:30.360
But the reconstruction defect

26:30.360 --> 26:32.040
is zero, because it still

26:32.040 --> 26:33.360
functions perfectly as my

26:33.360 --> 26:33.780
garage.

26:34.240 --> 26:35.360
It hasn't lost its identity.

26:35.360 --> 26:37.040
It's still distinguishable as

26:37.040 --> 26:37.660
a garage.

26:37.840 --> 26:39.020
But if a hurricane blows the

26:39.020 --> 26:40.620
roof off the garage, the

26:40.620 --> 26:41.940
defect is massive.

26:42.220 --> 26:42.640
Exactly.

26:43.260 --> 26:44.560
When the defect pushes the

26:44.560 --> 26:45.440
system below the

26:45.440 --> 26:47.080
admissibility threshold, the

26:47.080 --> 26:48.660
system must trigger a repair

26:48.660 --> 26:49.160
operator.

26:49.660 --> 26:51.340
But here is where Flyxion

26:51.340 --> 26:52.640
shatters our intuition.

26:53.560 --> 26:54.660
The mathematical objective

26:54.660 --> 26:56.620
of the repair operator is not

26:56.620 --> 26:57.860
to undo the damage and

26:57.860 --> 26:59.120
restore the system to the

26:59.120 --> 27:00.860
